WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.675
Fuel is the same arithmetic with higher stakes, and there’s a rule that has brought a lot of captains home.

2
00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:08.750
The rule of thirds.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.475
One third of your fuel to go out.

4
00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:13.725
One third to come back.

5
00:00:13.975 --> 00:00:16.375
And one third held in reserve.

6
00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:18.525
Work one on screen.

7
00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:23.075
Your spot is forty-two miles out, and you cruise at fourteen knots.

8
00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:25.475
That’s three hours each way.

9
00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.175
You burn eighteen gallons an hour.

10
00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:31.675
Three hours is fifty-four gallons, one way.

11
00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:34.200
Now apply the rule of thirds.

12
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.975
Fifty-four gallons is one third.

13
00:00:37.225 --> 00:00:40.025
So how much do you need aboard when you leave?

14
00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:43.050
Three times fifty-four.

15
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.775
One hundred sixty-two gallons.

16
00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:48.050
And that’s for a calm day.

17
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.050
Rough seas, head winds and heavy loads all burn more.

18
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.275
So be conservative.
